---
title: How to create a project and invoice, then invite the client to the portal once the invoice is paid
sidebar:
  order: 17
---
**A common setup: when a client says yes, Taskip creates their project and invoice for you. Once they pay that invoice, Taskip invites them to your client portal. Because a workflow can only do what its own category offers, this takes two short workflows that work together.**

### **Why two workflows?**

- **Each workflow belongs to one category** (Quotation, Document, Invoice and so on) and starts from one trigger.
- **“Invite to Client Portal” is an Invoice action.** You will not see it in the Quotation or Document builders.
- **A workflow can't pause until an invoice is paid.** Instead, a second workflow in the Invoice category starts by itself when the invoice is paid.

| | Workflow 1: Start | Workflow 2: Invite |
|---|---|---|
| **Category** | Quotation (or Document) | Invoice |
| **Trigger** | Quotation Accepted (or Document Fully Signed) | Invoice Paid |
| **Actions** | Convert To Invoice and Create Project (or Create Invoice and Create Project) | Invite to Client Portal |

### **Workflow 1: create the project and the invoice**

**Option A: start from an accepted quotation**

1. **On the left sidebar, click Workflow, then Create Workflow, then Start from Scratch.**
1. **Enter a Workflow Name, such as “Accepted quotation to project and invoice”.**
1. **Click the Quotation tab and choose the Quotation Accepted card** (“Trigger when a quotation is accepted by the client”). The trigger is chosen here, in this window.
1. **Click Create Workflow.** The workflow builder opens with your trigger already on the canvas.
1. **In the Workflow Nodes panel on the left, click Action to add an Action node, then drag from the bottom dot of the trigger to the top dot of the new action to connect them.**
1. **Click the Action node, set Action Type to Convert To Invoice, and click Save Configuration.** Nothing else needs to be filled in.
1. **Add a second Action node and connect it below the first.**
1. **Click it, set Action Type to Create Project, enter a Project Title, and click Save Configuration.** The title can use the quotation's details, for example `Project for {{quotation_no}}`.
1. **Click Save Changes, then switch the workflow from Paused to Active.**

**Option B: start from a signed document**

1. **Create a workflow and, on the Document tab, choose Document Fully Signed** (“Trigger when every signer has signed the document”).
1. **Add two actions: Create Invoice (set the Amount and Currency) and Create Project (set the Project Title).** Remember to click Save Configuration on each one.
1. **Click Save Changes and switch the workflow to Active.**

### **Workflow 2: invite the client when the invoice is paid**

1. **Click Create Workflow again, choose Start from Scratch, and enter a name such as “Invite client after payment”.**
1. **Click the Invoice tab and choose the Invoice Paid card** (“Trigger when an invoice is marked as paid”), then click Create Workflow.
1. **Click Action to add an Action node and connect it to the trigger.**
1. **Click the Action node, set Action Type to Invite to Client Portal, and click Save Configuration.** There is nothing else to set up. Taskip invites the client on the invoice, and skips anyone who already has portal access.
1. **Click Save Changes and switch the workflow to Active.**

### **Optional extras**

- **Condition:** in Workflow 2, add a Condition node so the invite only goes out when the invoice meets conditions you choose, such as its amount or contact.
- **Delay:** add a Delay node before the invite if you would like to wait, for example a day, after payment.
- **Paid by card or marked paid by hand:** Workflow 2 starts either way, whether the client pays online or you change the invoice status to Paid yourself.
- **Branding:** the page clients see when they open the invite can be customised under Settings → Client Portal → Client Invitation Page.

### **What happens end to end**

1. **The client accepts the quotation (or signs the document).**
1. **Workflow 1 runs: the project and the invoice are created.**
1. **The client pays the invoice.**
1. **Workflow 2 runs: the client receives their portal invitation.**

### **Good to know**

- **Workflow 2 runs for every invoice that is paid, not only the ones Workflow 1 created.** If you only want some invoices to trigger the invite, add a Condition node.
- **You can also invite a client by hand** from their Contact record at any time.
